    "q-122934": {
      "dom_id": "step-q122934",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[0,6]?$\n\nI. $0<2<4<8$\n\nII. $\\{0,3,6\\}$\n\nIII. $0<1<3<5<6$",
      "worked_solution": "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na={x}_{0}<{x}_{1}<{x}_{2}<…<{x}_{n}=b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{n}\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is not a partition of $[0,6]$ since $8$ does not belong to $[0,6].$\n\n- Statement II is a partition of $[0,6].$\n\n- Statement III is a partition of $[0,6].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
