    "q-122939": {
      "dom_id": "step-q122939",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[3,9]?$\n\nI. $\\{3,5,8,9\\}$\n\nII. $3<4<6<7<8$\n\nIII. $\\{1,3,4,8,9\\}$",
      "worked_solution": "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na={x}_{0}<{x}_{1}<{x}_{2}<…<{x}_{n}=b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{n}\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is a partition of $[3,9].$\n\n- Statement II is not a partition of $[3,9]$  since it does not include the right endpoint $b=9.$\n\n- Statement III is not a partition of $[3,9]$ since $1$ does not belong to $[3,9].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
