    "q-122927": {
      "dom_id": "step-q122927",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[0,9]?$\n\nI. $1<5<9$\n\nII. $0<5<7<9<10$\n\nIII. $\\{0,1,2,6,8,9\\}$",
      "worked_solution": "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na={x}_{0}<{x}_{1}<{x}_{2}<…<{x}_{n}=b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{n}\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is not a partition of $[0,9]$ since it does not include the left endpoint $a=0.$\n\n- Statement II is not a partition of $[0,9]$ since $10$ does not belong to $[0,9].$\n\n- Statement III is a partition of $[0,9].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
