    "q-122923": {
      "dom_id": "step-q122923",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[-2,6]?$\n\nI. $\\{-2,-1,0,6\\}$\n\nII. $\\{0,2,4,6\\}$\n\nIII. $-2<2<4<5$",
      "worked_solution": "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na={x}_{0}<{x}_{1}<{x}_{2}<…<{x}_{n}=b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{n}\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is a partition of $[-2,6].$\n\n- Statement II is not a partition of $[-2,6]$ since it does not include the left endpoint $a=-2.$\n\n- Statement III is not a partition of $[-2,6]$ since it does not include the right endpoint $b=6.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
