    "q-122974": {
      "dom_id": "step-q122974",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Let $P=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[5,14].$ If $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}-2Δ{y}_{j}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we take the factor $(-2)$ outside the summation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}-2Δ{y}_{j}=-2{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}$ is just the length of the interval $[5,14],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =({y}_{1}-{y}_{0})+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})+({y}_{3}-{y}_{2})+⋯+({y}_{n}-{y}_{n-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{y}_{1}}-{y}_{0})+(\\cancel{{y}_{2}}-\\cancel{{y}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{y}_{3}}-\\cancel{{y}_{2}})+⋯+({y}_{n}-\\cancel{{y}_{n-1}}) \\\\  & =-{y}_{0}+{y}_{n} \\\\  & ={y}_{n}-{y}_{0} \\\\  & =14-5 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n-2{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=(-2)\\cdot 9=-18.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
