    "q-122864": {
      "dom_id": "step-q122864",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Let $P=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[0,4].$ If $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}8({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the constant multiple rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}8({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j}=8{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the summation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j} & =({y}_{1}+{y}_{0})Δ{y}_{1}+({y}_{2}+{y}_{1})Δ{y}_{2}+⋯+({y}_{n}+{y}_{n-1})Δ{y}_{n} \\\\  & =({y}_{1}+{y}_{0})({y}_{1}-{y}_{0})+({y}_{2}+{y}_{1})({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})+⋯+({y}_{n}+{y}_{n-1})({y}_{n}-{y}_{n-1}) \\\\  & =({y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2})+({y}_{2}^{2}-{y}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{n-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{y}_{1}^{2}}-{y}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{y}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{y}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({y}_{n}^{2}-\\cancel{{y}_{n-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{y}_{0}^{2}+{y}_{n}^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${y}_{0}=0$ and ${y}_{n}=4$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j} & ={y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={4}^{2}-{0}^{2} \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n8{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j}=8\\cdot 16=128.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
