    "q-122991": {
      "dom_id": "step-q122991",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "Let $P=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[1,3].$ If $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}5({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the constant multiple rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}5({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}=5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}.\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the summation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{m} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${x}_{0}=1$ and ${x}_{m}=3$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={3}^{2}-{1}^{2} \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}=5\\cdot 8=40.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
