    "q-122987": {
      "dom_id": "step-q122987",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "Let $P=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[3,8].$ If $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}.$",
      "worked_solution": "We can simplify the given summation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{n} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${x}_{0}=3$ and ${x}_{m}=8$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={8}^{2}-{3}^{2} \\\\  & =55.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
